 <p class="text-lg text-slate-700 italic">For brands and importers, the OEM sweet spot is a <strong>10,000mAh power bank with 20-30W USB-C PD, MOQ 500, FOB $4-7/unit</strong>. The global market surpassed <strong>$16.4 billion in 2026</strong>, with Shenzhen producing over 80% of supply. New technologies, <strong>semi-solid-state batteries</strong>, <strong>Qi2 magnetic wireless</strong>, <strong>GaN V delivery</strong>, have reshaped the OEM landscape. This guide covers B2B sourcing fundamentals: <strong>capacity tier strategy with FOB pricing, MOQ flexibility from 500 units, certification requirements (CE/FCC/UL/UN38.3), Grade-A cell verification, and private label branding options</strong>, with real factory pricing from Shenzhen's manufacturing hub.</p>
