 <section id="faq" class="mb-16">
 <div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-2xl p-8 border border-slate-200 shadow-sm">
 <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-brandBlue uppercase italic mb-8 text-center">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
 <div class="space-y-6 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
 
 
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 faq-answer">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">What certifications do OEM importers need for power banks in the US and EU?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">EU: CE, RoHS, REACH, UN38.3 (lithium battery transport, included in CE/FCC/RoHS package at $2,500-4,500, 4-6 weeks), WEEE registration. US: FCC Part 15B, UN38.3, UL 2056 (power-bank-specific safety, strongly recommended at $3,000-8,000, 2-3 months). Japan: PSE. South Korea: KC. Budget $1,500-5,000 total for certification testing, plan 8-12 weeks for global market readiness. GB47372-2026 compliance is mandatory for factory export from China starting April 2027. Always verify certificates on the issuing body's public database, not just supplier-provided PDFs.</p>
 </div>
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 faq-answer">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">What MOQ and FOB pricing should OEM buyers expect for power bank orders?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">Laser engraving logo: MOQ 500 units. Silk screen logo: MOQ 1,000 units. Branding on in-stock models (ODM): MOQ <strong>500 units (laser logo) / 1,000 units (silk screen)</strong>. ODM with new design, not in stock: MOQ 1,000-2,000 units. Full OEM with new tooling: MOQ 3,000+ units. FOB Shenzhen pricing at 1,000 units: 5,000mAh ~$3-5, 10,000mAh ~$4.50-7, 20,000mAh ~$10-14, 27,000mAh ~$14-22. GaN circuit adds $1-3/unit; Qi2 wireless adds $2-4/unit. WOWOHCOOL offers flexible MOQ from 500 units with model mixing across SKUs. Payment terms: 30% deposit, 70% before shipment (T/T). Lead time: 25-30 days after sample approval.</p>
 </div>
 
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 faq-answer">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">What wattage and port configuration sells best for OEM power banks in 2026?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">USB-C PD is the mandatory baseline: 65W covers ~85% of ultrabooks, 140W PD 3.1 EPR covers all laptops. The 2C1A (2× USB-C + 1× USB-A) port layout is the 2026 standard. Qi2 magnetic wireless adds $2-4 to BOM but enables a premium SKU tier. Built-in cables are a niche differentiation feature. The optimal mass-market SKU: 10,000mAh, 65W GaN, 2C1A, digital battery display. The premium-tier SKU: 20,000mAh, 140W PD 3.1 EPR, Qi2 magnetic wireless, TFT display.</p>
 </div>
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 faq-answer">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">How do OEM buyers ship power banks internationally, UN38.3, IATA, and dangerous goods rules?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">Power banks are Class 9 Dangerous Goods (UN3480/UN3481). Requirements: UN38.3 test certification (mandatory, $2,000-4,000, 4-6 weeks), MSDS documentation, batteries must ship at ≤30% charge state per IATA. ≤100Wh (~27,000mAh): standard DG cargo with proper labeling, carry-on without airline approval. 100-160Wh: airline approval required, max 2 units. >160Wh: prohibited on passenger aircraft. Logistics costs are 25-40% higher than standard electronics due to DG surcharges. Never ship undeclared lithium batteries, fines start at $50,000 per violation.</p>
 </div>
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 faq-answer">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">How do OEM buyers start sourcing power banks from Shenzhen factories?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm"><strong>Step 1:</strong> Define the target market, retail price point, and capacity, this determines certifications and BOM. <strong>Step 2:</strong> Choose from 29+ existing OEM power bank models or request custom ODM. <strong>Step 3:</strong> Request 3-5 production-grade samples (3-7 day turnaround) and test actual capacity, charging speed, and build quality. <strong>Step 4:</strong> Finalize branding and packaging, pay 30% deposit, production begins (25-30 days). <strong>Step 5:</strong> Use a lithium-battery-specialist forwarder for DG-compliant shipping. <strong><a href="/contact/" class="text-brandOrange hover:underline">Request a no-obligation OEM quote with current FOB pricing and lead times →</a></strong></p>
